  {
   "id": "cb_0c0dc1b8acb821cfac4c823b",
   "order": 13,
   "title_en": "Considerations",
   "body_en": "1. Please set the plate type to Smooth PEI/High Temp Plate and carefully follow the Heatbed Recommended Settings when using the Bambu 3D Effect Plate. For X1/X2/P2 Series users, please disable the Build Plate Position Detection in 'Settings ->Print Options -> Enable the detection of build plate position' when printing with the 3D Effect Plate to avoid error reports.\n2. The 3D effect patterns require a clean surface to remain visible. Grease can cause the patterns to disappear. It is essential to keep the surface clean. We recommend using hot water and detergent for cleaning, and avoid touching the surface.\n3. Due to reflections, the LIDAR calibration will not work as expected when using Effect Plates. We recommend skipping the LIDAR calibration sequence, or calibrating with a regular plate.\n4. The 3D Effect Plates are considered consumables. To prolong the lifespan of the transfer textures, try placing your print objects on different areas of the sheet.\n5. Do not apply glue to the plate surface.\n6. Pay close attention when using a scraper to remove prints, to avoid damaging the plate surface.",
   "url": "",
   "source_media_id": "",
   "source_url": "",
   "alt_en": "",
   "alt_ar": "",
   "alt_ckb": "",
   "kind": "text",
   "section_kind": "overview",
   "section_path": "html › 6"
  },
  {
   "id": "cb_a05c9165e3ef53a0262e13da",
   "order": 14,
   "title_en": "Recommended Settings",
   "body_en": "We recommend using PLA and TPU filament for printing. Please note that other slicer settings might need to be adjusted based on the printed model and the filament requirements. Please select Smooth PEI Plate/High Temp Plate for the Plate Type in Bambu Studio.\nFilaments | Heatbed Temperature\nPLA | 60~65℃\nTPU | 35~45℃",
   "url": "",
   "source_media_id": "",
   "source_url": "",
   "alt_en": "",
   "alt_ar": "",
   "alt_ckb": "",
   "kind": "text",
   "section_kind": "overview",
   "section_path": "html › 7"
  }
